maria (docs): Quick heads-up — PR #412 touched the function/tool-calling examples and introduced an ambiguous nullable-array example. Link checker failed on one anchor. Can we triage?

alex (sdk): I can add a JS SDK snippet clarifying empty-array vs null semantics. Quick question: do we prefer normalizing empty responses to [] or preserving null to indicate 'no value'?

sam (eng): Preserve semantic distinction (null != []). But SDK helper can offer opt-in normalization. I'll add a flag like `normalizeEmptyArrays` default false.

maria (docs): That sounds good. Also the docs linter flagged /guides/tool-calling#schema -> 404. @kevin (product) is that an expected rename?

kevin (product): Yeah that anchor moved in the site refactor. We should add a redirect from /guides/tool-calling#schema -> /reference/tool-calling#json-schema. Not blocking, will land a redirect in the next deploy.

alex (sdk): Proposed JS snippet — short example showing parsing a tool response with a nullable array field and an SDK helper: 

```js
// sdk usage: request structured output from model and coerce empty list if desired
const resp = await redwoodClient.generate({
  input: prompt,
  outputSchema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {
      results: { type: ['array', 'null'], items: { type: 'string' }, nullable: true }
    },
  },
  normalizeEmptyArrays: true // optional SDK helper flag
});

// SDK post-process: if normalizeEmptyArrays && resp.results == null -> resp.results = []
```

maria (docs): Nice, please add a one-line migration note: "If you previously relied on null to signal absence, keep behavior by not enabling normalizeEmptyArrays." Also we need a small Python example snippet for the migration guide.

alex (sdk): Python snippet — quick draft: 

```py
# python sdk: parse tool output, optional normalization
resp = client.generate(input=prompt, output_schema={
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "results": {"type": ["array", "null"], "items": {"type": "string"}}
  }
}, normalize_empty_arrays=True)

if resp["results"] is None:
    resp["results"] = []
```

sam (eng): I'll add runtime compatibility tests to accept both `[]` and `null` for tool outputs coming from older models. Also will add an explicit schema example in the guide that uses "type": ["array", "null"] and a short note about `nullable` vs union types.

maria (docs): I'm patching PR description with the migration guidance and linking the SDK snippets. Also flagged in PR checklist: update changelog entry and add a short automated test snippet for the docs (curl + sample response).

docs-bot: Automated check: 1 broken link remaining -> /guides/tool-calling#schema?version=old

maria (docs): Ugh, still one leftover anchor with query param. I'll push a tiny redirect commit and rerun link-check.

docs-bot: Suggested replacement: /reference/tool-calling#json-schema (detected best match)

maria (docs): Thanks. I'll push redirect and request review from @alex (sdk) and @sam (eng). Also proposing a 1-line migration banner at the top of the tool-calling guide explaining the optional SDK flag.

alex (sdk): :thumbsup: will review after lunch. I'll make the JS snippet idiomatic and include a short test harness.

sam (eng): I'll add the runtime tests by EOD and open a tiny PR to the runtime repo referencing this docs PR.

kevin (product): Great. One ask: if we ever flip default behavior in the future, make sure SDK changelog/top-level release notes call it out as a breaking behavior. For now opt-in is fine.

maria (docs): No default change — opt-in only. Tagging this thread as docs-pr/docs-sprint. I'll update the PR title once the redirect lands and remove the broken-link CI failure.

alex (sdk): noted. I'll also add a short snippet to the SDK README under "Parsing tool outputs" so examples are discoverable.

sam (eng): Follow-up: when we add runtime tests, I'll include a quick fuzz case where model returns "results": null vs "results": [] to ensure deterministic downstream behavior.

maria (docs): Perfect. Thanks everyone — back to prep the migration blurb. Ping when reviews are in and I'll merge after redirect is live.

kevin (product): Thanks all.
